<title>USA: Halliburton unit loses major contract - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Halliburton unit loses major contract - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>DynCorp has won a major defense contract to provide logistical support for the U.S. military, beating Halliburton's Brown &amp; Root unit, the Wall Street Journal said Monday.</p>
<p>The paper said the contract has an explicit value of only $25 million, but that the implementation of the contract's plans, such as providing meals and hauling garbage, will provide a large amount of revenue to closely held DynCorp.</p>
<p>DynCorp of Reston, Virginia, provides maintenance service around the world to the U.S. military, the report said.</p>
</text>
